; The 512 fallback (plan 08, "The 512 fallback").
;
; pacer holds MAX_TEMPO_SEGMENTS = 512 tempo segments. Adjacent equal
; tempi coalesce always; past the cap, segments within `--tempo-eps`
; coalesce too; and if even that is not enough the table is DROPPED and
; every position prints in SECONDS off the real tempo map, with
; `export_tempo_budget`.
;
; Six hundred segments one whole quarter-note-per-minute apart is the
; third case: nothing coalesces at the default `--tempo-eps` of 0.01, and
; six hundred is out of pacer's reach. The piece still sounds right; its
; beat lanes run on the transport's one tempo.
;
; The points are one sixteenth note apart and were written by a script,
; which is the only file in this corpus that was: six hundred lines of
; the same form is a quantity, not a text, and the quantity IS the case.
(timeline :title "slide" :length 64bar)

(meter-point :at 0bar :sig [4 4])

(tempo-point :at 0t :qpm 60)
